  "planning_notes": [
    "Business logic for state classification (normal/overload/overheat/mechanical abnormality), thresholds, and how current/temperature/vibration map to state_code and fault_code are not specified in the prompt and must be implemented in the SysML model.",
    "Current sensor conversion from A0 ADC counts to amperes requires electrical calibration parameters (scale/offset) that are not provided; model should apply calibration and report in A.",
    "LM35 conversion from A1 ADC counts to degC requires scale/offset parameters that are not provided; model should apply conversion and report in degC.",
    "D2 vibration switch polarity: the prompt does not state active level or pullup wiring; a conservative assumption active_high=true and pullup=false is used in the digital_input request. If the hardware is active-low, invert in the model or adjust request.",
    "Fan PWM D5: PWM enable strategy (e.g., continuous when overheat, or duty proportional to temperature) is not specified; PWM output is provided and SysML determines its duty.",
    "TM1637 display rotation timing (\"轮流显示\" cadence among current, temperature, and state number) and mapping to displayed integers are model responsibilities; TM1637 port supports an integer value only.",
    "Serial protocol details (exact message format/text or fixed line requirements) are not specified; therefore this interface proposal uses typed numeric reports under one periodic gate. If a fixed exact text line is required, replace/add with serial_text_output entries at the same baud."
  ],
